        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/3 Adenocarcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68285,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C27.0 &amp; XH74S1 Carcinoma of thymus &amp; Adenocarcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68286,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> non-mucinous adenocarcinoma; tubular adenocarcinoma; tubulopapillary carcinoma; high-grade papillary carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68287,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68288,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenocarcinoma NOS of the thymus is localized in the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T11:40:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68289,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients either present with symptoms related to the thymic mass lesion or are asymptomatic {23725376}. Lymph node and distant metastases are common. Paraneoplastic syndromes have not been described.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>The imaging features of adenocarcinoma NOS of the thymus are similar to those of other thymic carcinomas {12502935; 15754301}. Whole-body FDG&nbsp;PET-CT is helpful to exclude metastasis from a primary elsewhere.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68290,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Thymic adenocarcinomas are rare, with approximately 70&nbsp;cases having been reported in the literature {29339175}. In the International Thymic Malignancy Interest Group (ITMIG) cohort, only 11 of 706&nbsp;patients (1.6%) with thymic epithelial malignancy (carcinoma) have thymic adenocarcinoma {28038793}. The mean age is 45&nbsp;years {29339175}. Males predominate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68291,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68292,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68293,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumours are usually large, soft, and invasive, measuring 50&ndash;140 mm in greatest dimension. Necrosis, cystic changes, and mucinous areas can be present {29339175}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-03T11:10:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68294,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "<p>Provisionally, adenocarcinoma NOS includes tubular adenocarcinoma, non-mucinous adenocarcinoma, high-grade papillary adenocarcinoma, and signet-ring cell carcinoma with a gastric immunophenotype. Histologically, the tumours show variable combinations of tubules and tubulopapillary structures lined by columnar cells {16959713; 22407350}. Mucinous areas may be present. Rarely, a solid component is present, with sheets of neoplastic cells and only a limited glandular component. Nuclear pleomorphism and coagulative necrosis are common {29339175}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Adenocarcinomas NOS are positive for pancytokeratins and sometimes also CD5. By definition, they lack expression of enteric markers (CK20, CDX2, and MUC2) {16959713; 12502935; 23725376}. Other markers, such as CEA or CA19-9, may be positive {23725376; 23110032}. Some cases express CK7 {15754301; 17721187; 30259765}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:05:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68295,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not available</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68296,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68297,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Adenocarcinoma of thymus after exclusion of mediastinal metastasis from other sites and defined types of thymic adenocarcinoma (low-grade papillary, enteric-type)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Immunophenotyping to rule out mediastinal metastasis or defined types of thymic adenocarcinoma</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T17:12:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68298,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenocarcinomas NOS should be staged according to the TNM system [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]] {25396314} and, optionally, the Masaoka&ndash;Koga system {21847052}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:06:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68299,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 242,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenocarcinomas NOS tend to be advanced-stage and aggressive tumours, with poor prognosis {23725376}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T09:53:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]